{
	title: 'Schedule round calls by read-only status',
	spec: "Only wholly read-only non-WAIT work in one model round runs concurrently. Any effectful call makes all non-WAIT calls sequential in original order across native call boundaries. WAIT always starts last after all other calls settle, including within compound calls; results return in original call order. Per-call state is per call, never per session: foreground bash output streams per call (snapshots carry every running call's partial output), every running call flagged unsafeToStop is tracked, a deferred steer interrupts once none of them still runs, and a restart lists them all. A model-run command names its own executing call (Sender.call) instead of relying on the session status, which names only the latest started call. Approval questions, steering cancellation, /clear before dispatch and declined calls keep their per-call results.",
